prompt_template:
Create one finished editorial campaign poster. Prioritized visual system:
{STYLE_FIDELITY_ANCHORS}
Photographic subject and pose: {SUBJECT}
Compact block headline, verbatim: "{MAIN_TEXT}".
Words building the body silhouette, verbatim in this reading order: "{BODY_TEXT}".
Small red handwritten supporting line, verbatim: "{SECONDARY_TEXT}".
Art direction: {DESIGN_DIRECTION}
Source content exclusions: {SOURCE_CONTENT_TO_AVOID}
The letters replace the torso rather than sitting on a photographed garment: no shirt seams, no fabric, no border or solid backing panel under them. Pale gaps between letters match the surrounding background. Facial anatomy, hands and feet remain photographic and coherent. Fine restrained photographic grain, natural skin, soft diffuse studio light, faint grounding shadow; slight organic marker edges. Keep every word readable. Borderless poster, no mockup, no additional copy.
Critical execution: body words must be THIN, LONG, LOOSE HANDWRITING with open spaces, not solid fat black letter blocks. The ghost torso is the SAME gray-white photographic background visible between and outside letters, with no white fabric perimeter. Let outer letters taper and stagger individually. Preserve a coherent figurative collage, not a visibly cut-out white bodysuit. Keep a small compact headline and broad quiet margins; the person need not fill the entire frame.
